WEBVTT

1
00:00:03.400 --> 00:00:06.600
Every specimen Cajal studied was fixed.

2
00:00:07.280 --> 00:00:13.060
A row of fibres of different lengths could show stages of one fibre growing,

3
00:00:13.060 --> 00:00:14.320
or old fibres becoming visible.

4
00:00:15.520 --> 00:00:18.580
Someone had to watch a fibre while it was alive.

5
00:00:19.640 --> 00:00:24.440
Inside a living animal, that is hard, and so is changing one thing at a time.

6
00:00:25.333 --> 00:00:28.313
Take a piece of tissue at a chosen stage.

7
00:00:29.453 --> 00:00:33.873
Harrison removed frog neural tube before any nerve fibres could be seen.

8
00:00:34.633 --> 00:00:38.713
He set it in a drop of fresh adult frog lymph on a coverslip.

9
00:00:39.553 --> 00:00:42.953
The lymph clotted into a soft mesh that held the tissue.

10
00:00:43.873 --> 00:00:47.973
Then he inverted the coverslip over a hollow slide and sealed it.

11
00:00:48.893 --> 00:00:52.053
Tissue kept alive outside the body is an explant.

12
00:00:52.867 --> 00:00:56.267
In culture, cells need a solid to move on.

13
00:00:57.047 --> 00:01:00.367
Harrison saw frog cells wander along spider-web threads.

14
00:01:01.307 --> 00:01:06.627
To watch single neurons, break tissue into single cells and plate them thinly, so

15
00:01:06.627 --> 00:01:07.647
each can be followed.

16
00:01:08.727 --> 00:01:13.627
Banker and Cowan used fetal rat hippocampus, on polylysine-treated coverslips.

17
00:01:14.627 --> 00:01:17.467
Cells plated straight from tissue make a primary culture.

18
00:01:18.300 --> 00:01:20.800
The medium is part of the experiment.

19
00:01:21.760 --> 00:01:27.860
Eagle found 12 amino acid compounds necessary for growth of HeLa cells, a cell line.

20
00:01:28.500 --> 00:01:31.060
A continuous line can divide indefinitely.

21
00:01:32.360 --> 00:01:33.400
Partners can be added too.

22
00:01:34.420 --> 00:01:39.640
Isolated hippocampal neurons survived only a few days, but with hippocampal

23
00:01:39.640 --> 00:01:41.800
explants alongside, about two weeks.

24
00:01:42.440 --> 00:01:43.720
That is a coculture.

25
00:01:44.583 --> 00:01:50.183
To read a halo, look at the fibres around a ganglion after about a day.

26
00:01:51.023 --> 00:01:54.243
Their density shows how much factor a sample holds.

27
00:01:55.123 --> 00:01:59.023
The highest dilution that still gives a halo gives the activity.

28
00:02:00.003 --> 00:02:05.703
In this idealised example, the halo shrinks as the sample is diluted, and the most

29
00:02:05.703 --> 00:02:07.183
dilute dish gives none.

30
00:02:08.017 --> 00:02:09.917
Culture can mislead.

31
00:02:10.877 --> 00:02:17.217
Mycoplasma escapes detection by turbidity or ordinary microscopy, and resists common

32
00:02:17.217 --> 00:02:21.217
antibiotics. Compare with mycoplasma-free lines.

33
00:02:22.257 --> 00:02:28.217
Identity can be wrong: Gartler reported apparent HeLa contamination of other human

34
00:02:28.217 --> 00:02:35.497
lines in 1968. DNA fingerprinting by STR profiling was reproducible between

35
00:02:35.497 --> 00:02:38.577
laboratories, across 253 lines.

36
00:02:39.377 --> 00:02:45.697
And a line differs from tissue: the HeLa Kyoto genome shows extensive aneuploidy.

37
00:02:46.367 --> 00:02:52.987
In the early 1900s, Harrison watched fibres grow from tissue taken before fibres

38
00:02:52.987 --> 00:02:59.247
existed. The clot held no chain of cells, and some fibres arose from a single

39
00:02:59.407 --> 00:03:04.947
isolated cell. He concluded that an axon is drawn out from one cell.

40
00:03:06.047 --> 00:03:12.587
In the early 1950s, in Rio de Janeiro, Levi-Montalcini cultured chick ganglia beside

41
00:03:12.587 --> 00:03:16.327
tumour fragments and saw a halo of fibres within a day.

42
00:03:17.007 --> 00:03:21.727
That halo became the bioassay used to purify nerve growth factor.

43
00:03:22.500 --> 00:03:28.840
In 2000, Scheiffele and colleagues found that neuroligin on a non-neuronal cell

44
00:03:28.840 --> 00:03:33.060
triggers presynaptic differentiation in contacting axons.

45
00:03:33.860 --> 00:03:38.040
A partner cell with no other synaptic machinery made that possible.

46
00:03:38.920 --> 00:03:44.800
Yet mice lacking neuroligins 1 to 3 had synapses in normal number in the brainstem,

47
00:03:44.800 --> 00:03:46.460
with impaired transmission.

48
00:03:47.260 --> 00:03:52.880
Keep this rule: sufficient in a dish does not mean required in the animal.
